UID:160cbaa16b7358da@role-environmental-land-use.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260915T114050Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Fall 2026
DESCRIPTION:Nonpoint Source Training News - Fall 2026\nMaine Department of
  Environmental Protection sent this bulletin at 09/10/2026 02:48 PM EDT\nS
 eptember 2026\nIn this Issue:\nFall and Winter Classes for Re-Certificatio
 n\nOUR SHORE Reference Guide Now Available!\n2nd Annual OUR SHORE Practiti
 oner Roundtable October 27th in Orono\nFall and Winter Classes for Re-Cert
 ification\nMany Erosion Control Certifications will be expiring for indivi
 duals at the end of December\, and continuing education hours are required
  to keep your certification current. You don’t have to wait until expira
 tion to take classes\, so even if you expire in 2026\, you can still get r
 ecertification credits.\nAs we approach the end of the year\, we encourage
  certified individuals to check their certification expirations and contac
 t information for accuracy. You can check your certification status here:\
 nNPS Training Center - Certified Contractor List\, Maine Department of Env
 ironmental Protection.\nOnline and in-person classes are posted here:\nTra
 ining Schedule and Courses\, Nonpoint Source Training & Resource Center\, 
 Maine DEP\nPlease send any updates to\nNPSTraining.DEP@maine.gov\n.\nThe N
 PSTC will be offering in-person trainings statewide this fall and winter\,
  with more being added in other locations over time. For anyone recertifyi
 ng\, we highly encourage taking classes you have not yet attended (instead
  of attending the introductory class again). We partner with towns and non
 profits to offer these trainings across the state\, so reach out if you’
 d like to assist in setting up a training in your area.\nOUR SHORE Referen
 ce Guide Now Available!\nThe OUR SHORE Reference Guide is complete. The OU
 R SHORE Program and Reference Guide reflect a collective commitment to sho
 reline resilience and environmental protection. Critical contributions of 
 individuals from state and federal agencies\, nongovernmental organization
 s\, municipalities\, and shoreline stabilization engineers\, designers\, l
 andscape architects\, and earthworks contractors cre\nhttps://content.govd
 elivery.com/accounts/MEDEP/bulletins/42979e0
URL:https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/MEDEP/bulletins/42979e0
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
