UID:96966770dfad3fdf@role-environmental-land-use.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260910T205020Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260910
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Maine DEP\, MRRA and MSW Consultants Announce
  Waste Characterization Study Webinar
DESCRIPTION:Maine DEP\, MRRA and MSW Consultants Announce Waste Characteri
 zation Study Webinar\nMaine Department of Environmental Protection sent th
 is bulletin at 09/09/2026 04:30 PM EDT\n--- PRESS RELEASE ---\nFor Immedia
 te Release\nMaine DEP\, MRRA and MSW Consultants Announce Waste Characteri
 zation Study Webinar\nAUGUSTA\, September 9\, 2026\n— The Maine Departme
 nt of Environmental Protection (DEP) is partnering with the Maine Resource
  Recovery Association (MRRA) and MSW Consultants to provide a live webinar
  and Q&A session presenting the results of the recently completed statewid
 e waste characterization study.  The study\, commissioned by the DEP and 
 funded entirely through the USEPA's Solid Waste Infrastructure for Recycli
 ng (SWIFR) grant program\, provides a detailed analysis on the composition
  of Maine’s waste stream. The full study is available on the\nDepartment
  Reports webpage\n.\nThe webinar will take place on September 15\nth\n\, 2
 026 from 12:00pm to 2:00pm and will include a robust review of the study d
 ata\, methodology\, and key findings.\nThe webinar will provide ample time
  for questions and discussion with the experts at MSW Consultants who cond
 ucted hands-on research and data analysis of Maine’s waste streams and a
 uthored the waste characterization study.\nRegister for the webinar at MRR
 A’s website:\nhttps://mrra.net/event/webinar-maines-waste-characterizati
 on-study/\nFor additional information\, contact\n:\nDavid R. Madore\, Depu
 ty Commissioner\ndavid.madore@maine.gov\nMaine Department of Environmental
  Protection\nManage Subscriber Preferences\n|\nUnsubscribe\n|\nHelp\n|\nCo
 ntact Us\nSTAY CONNECTED:\nhttps://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/MEDEP/
 bulletins/42943a2
URL:https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/MEDEP/bulletins/42943a2
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:c996128945bc06ec@role-environmental-land-use.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260910T162239Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260910
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Maine Wasted Food Prevention Week - September
  28 through October 4
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, food is one of Maine’s most valuable resources a
 nd is essential for the health and nutrition of all our 1.4 million reside
 nts\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, nearly 40 percent of food produced in Maine is neve
 r eaten – over 361\,000 tons annually – primarily ending up in landfil
 ls where it produces dangerous methane gas which is 28 times more potent t
 han carbon dioxide and a major contributor to climate change\; and\nWHEREA
 S\n\, Maine people can save money by preventing wasted food\, with the ave
 rage Maine family spending nearly $3\,000 annually on food that is thrown 
 away\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, over 80 percent of consumers misunderstand food da
 te labels causing large amounts of perfectly good food to be thrown away i
 n homes\, businesses\, and even food pantries\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Maine com
 munities can substantially reduce their waste disposal costs by preventing
  wasted food since food is the single largest municipal solid waste compon
 ent\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Maine K-12 schools have a special role in educating
  our next generation to reduce\, recover\, and recycle the estimated 7 mil
 lion pounds of school food wasted annually\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, we can help 
 our farmers\, strengthen our local food systems\, and conserve our natural
  resources – water\, air\, energy\, and land – by valuing Maine food a
 nd composting food scraps instead of wasting it as trash\;\nNOW THEREFORE\
 n\, be it resolved that I\, Janet T. Mills\, Governor of the State of Main
 e\, do hereby proclaim the week of September 28-October 4\, 2026\, as\nMai
 ne Wasted Food Prevention Week\nand I encourage all Maine people to become
  aware of the wasted food in our homes\, schools and all around us\, and t
 o commit to stop throwing food away.\nIn testimony whereof\, I have caused
 \nthe Great Seal of the State to be\nhereunto affixed GIVEN under my\nhand
  at Augusta this second day\nof September Two Thousand Twenty-Six\nhttp://
 www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2026-09-main
 e-wasted-food-prevention-week-september-28-through
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-09-maine-wasted-food-prevention-week-september-28-through
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
